## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a CAPA system for data-drift scenarios in a multi-tenant ML/PL workflow, bridging data, observability, and risk controls.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model with evidence linkage and drift metrics for traceability
- Lifecycle state machine with clear transitions and SLAs
- REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked logs/traces
- Tenant-aware metrics to prove containment and avoid recurrence
- RCA template and a staged canary rollback plan for feature-store changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// TypeScript interfaces for CAPA data model
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  tenant_id: string;
  feature_set: string;
  model_version: string;
  drift_score: { KL: number; KS: number; Wasserstein?: number };
  evidence_logs: string[];
  traces: string[];
  status: 'Detected'|'Investigating'|'Contained'|'Verified'|'Closed';
  created_at: string;
  updated_at: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale drift detection for thousands of tenants without increasing false positives?
- How would CAPA decisions be audited and rollback actions validated in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?
